Canadian Prairies QSO Party -- the 65 federal electoral districts (Alberta 37, Saskatchewan 14, Manitoba 14).
Codes and names from the sponsor table (docs/ContestRules/QSOParties/CanadianPrairies/canadian-prairies-districts.md, issue 117).
Each line maps its district to its province with a greater-than sign. Out of the prairies each district is its own multiplier
(FCONTEST sets MultipliersIsCounties). In the prairies a district counts as its province, and the ADIF STATE of a district is that province.
No INCLUDE here: an out-of-area entrant table must hold only districts. No line of this header may hold an equals sign.

